AR, Gibbons CM, Torres J, et al. Access to dermatological care with an innovative Online model for psoriasis management: results from a randomized controlled trial. Telemed J E Health. 2019;25(7):619–627. doi: 10.1089/tmj.2018.0160. [ DOI ] [ PMC free article ] [ PubMed ] [ Google Scholar ] 16. Frühauf J, Kröck S, Quehenberger F, et al. Mobile teledermatology helping patients control high-need acne: a randomized controlled trial. J Eur Acad Dermatol Venereol. 2015;29(5):919–924. doi: 10.1111/jdv.12723. [ DOI ] [ PubMed ] [ Google Scholar ] 17. Harst L, Otto L, Timpel P, et al. An empirically sound telemedicine taxonomy—applying the CAFE methodology. J Public Health. 2021 doi: 10.1007/s10389-021-01558-2. [ DOI ] [ Google Scholar ] 18. Henes FO, Stappenbeck P, Tahir E, et al. Implementation of a 24-hour teleradiology service for cruise ships: a pilot study. AJR Am J Roentgenol. 2020;214(4):754–760. doi: 10.2214/AJR.19.21794. [ DOI ] [ PubMed ] [ Google Scholar ] 19. Keppler K, Stöver H, Schulte B, et al. Prison Health is Public Health! Angleichungs- und Umsetzungsprobleme in der gesundheitlichen Versorgung Gefangener im deutschen Justizvollzug Ein Ubersichtsbeitrag. Bundesgesundheitsblatt Gesundheitsforschung Gesundheitsschutz. 2010;53(2):233–244. doi: 10.1007/s00103-009-1023-1. [ DOI ] [ PubMed ] [ Google Scholar ] 20. Kim GE, Afanasiev OK, O’Dell C, et al. Implementation and evaluation of Stanford Health Care store-and-forward teledermatology consultation workflow built within an existing electronic health record system. J Telemed Telecare. 2020;26(3):125–131. doi: 10.1177/1357633X18799805. [ DOI ] [ PubMed ] [ Google Scholar ] 21. Mehta SJ. Telemedicine’s potential ethical pitfalls. Virtual Mentor. 2014;16(12):1014–1017. doi: 10.1001/virtualmentor.2014.16.12.msoc1-1412. [ DOI ] [ PubMed ] [ Google Scholar ] 22. Nouri S, Khoong EC, Lyles CR et al (2020) Addressing equity in telemedicine for chronic disease management during the Covid-19 pandemic. https://catalyst.ne