urvey reported having stable housing (85.2% [23] vs 63.0% [68]; P = .04), having food security (63.0% [17] vs 38.0% [41]; P = .03), and completing 12 or more years of schooling (96.3% [26] vs 79.6% [86]; P = .05) ( Table 3 ). Table 3. Characteristics of Survey + Interview Participants and Survey-Only Participants. Characteristic Total No. (%) Survey-only participants, No. (%) Survey + interview participants, No. (%) P value All participants 135 (100) 108 (80.0) 27 (20.0) Age, y 18-44 40 (29.6) 33 (30.6) 7 (25.9) .61 45-64 68 (50.4) 55 (50.9) 13 (48.1) ≥65 26 (19.3) 19 (17.6) 7 (25.9) Missing data 1 (0.7) 1 (0.9) 0 Gender identity a Male 73 (54.1) 57 (52.8) 16 (59.3) .48 Female 52 (38.5) 43 (39.8) 9 (33.3) Transgender male or man 1 (0.7) 1 (0.9) 0 Transgender female or woman 3 (2.2) 3 (2.8) 0 Genderqueer or gender nonconforming 2 (1.5) 1 (0.9) 1 (3.7) Different identity 2 (1.5) 1 (0.9) 1 (3.7) Missing data 2 (1.5) 2 (1.9) 0 Race and ethnicity a Hispanic or Latino b 37 (27.4) 34 (31.5) 3 (11.1) .19 Non-Hispanic Asian c 13 (9.6) 10 (9.3) 3 (11.1) Non-Hispanic Black or African American 12 (8.9) 8 (7.4) 4 (14.8) Non-Hispanic White 49 (36.3) 37 (34.3) 12 (44.4) Other d 14 (10.4) 11 (10.2) 3 (11.1) Missing data 10 (7.4) 8 (7.4) 2 (7.4) Educational level, y <12 22 (16.3) 21 (19.4) 1 (3.7) .05 ≥12 112 (83.0) 86 (79.6) 26 (96.3) Missing data 1 (0.7) 1 (0.9) 0 Preferred language English 107 (79.3) 80 (74.1) 27 (100) .005 e Spanish 20 (14.8) 20 (18.5) 0 Cantonese 8 (5.9) 8 (7.4) 0 Length of time receiving care at this dermatology clinic, y <1 60 (44.4) 48 (44.4) 12 (44.4) .19 1 to <3 24 (17.8) 19 (17.6) 5 (18.5) 3 to <5 18 (13.3) 11 (10.2) 7 (25.9) ≥5 29 (21.5) 26 (24.1) 3 (11.1) Missing data 4 (3.0) 4 (3.7) 0 Self-reported health Excellent 15 (11.1) 12 (11.1) 3 (11.1) .55 Very good 26 (19.3) 21 (19.4) 5 (18.5) Good 50 (37.0) 42 (38.9) 8 (29.6) Fair 31 (23.0) 25 (23.1) 6 (22.2) Poor 10 (7.4) 6 (5.6) 4 (14.8) Missing data 3 (2.2) 2 (1.9) 1 (3.7) Housing instability Stable housin